Yeah!

00:01:48.753 --> 00:01:50.069
There's still a few more episodes before--

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:51.591
- Yeah, you need to get the cadence down.

00:01:51.591 --> 00:01:53.995
- [Voiceover] Andrew
asks "What do you think

00:01:53.995 --> 00:01:57.079
"of Snapchat's move to
charge for re-plays?"

00:01:57.079 --> 00:01:59.277
- Great question, I'm sure
it's on everybody's mind.

00:01:59.277 --> 00:02:00.800
I'm sure, you know, Staphon real quick,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.152
I think we should settle
this out into its own video.

00:02:03.152 --> 00:02:05.663
This is a very intriguing thing.

00:02:05.663 --> 00:02:09.257
This charging for the replays on Snapchat.

00:02:09.257 --> 00:02:12.306
To me, this feels tactical.

00:02:12.306 --> 00:02:15.151
What I mean by that is I do not believe

00:02:15.151 --> 00:02:16.352
that the powers at Snapchat,

00:02:16.352 --> 00:02:17.674
I have no knowledge of this,

00:02:17.674 --> 00:02:21.664
think this is a big time
revenue source for them.

00:02:21.664 --> 00:02:23.101
I think what Snapchat,

00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:25.451
I'm so impressed with Snapchat

00:02:25.451 --> 00:02:27.713
that they know they need to stay fresh.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:28.967
Right, we've also got that.

00:02:28.967 --> 00:02:29.972
Are you going to ask the question later

00:02:29.972 --> 00:02:31.992
about the new selfie thing?

00:02:31.992 --> 00:02:33.066
- [Steve] No, I was
just going to leave it--

00:02:33.066 --> 00:02:33.809
- Cool.

00:02:33.809 --> 00:02:35.419
So I'll use that in my answer.

00:02:35.419 --> 00:02:39.204
I think technology companies
need to have updates.

00:02:39.204 --> 00:02:40.988
Need to stay fresh.

00:02:40.988 --> 00:02:43.253
And I think Facebook
did that extremely well.

00:02:43.253 --> 00:02:44.996
And honestly, over the last half decade,

00:02:44.996 --> 00:02:46.762
you know especially the
last three or four years

00:02:46.762 --> 00:02:48.542
I think Twitter did that poorly.

00:02:48.542 --> 00:02:50.723
I think Instagram's
showing that capability.

00:02:50.723 --> 00:02:52.178
Different filters, different size.

00:02:52.178 --> 00:02:53.992
Even if it's not a big deal.

00:02:53.992 --> 00:02:56.175
And Snapchat is showing that ability.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.105
With Snapcash if you remember.

00:02:58.105 --> 00:02:59.429
And that's not the biggest
thing in the world.

00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:01.169
I think it's a quick little play.

00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:05.091
Clearly look, they're trying
to position towards an IPO,

00:03:05.091 --> 00:03:06.860
and so here's what I
think the strategy is.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.713
One, we make the users of Snapchat

00:03:08.713 --> 00:03:11.060
feel like there's still
things going on, right?

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.200
The new selfie filter thing which is wild.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.977
I mean, we might as well just do it here.

00:03:14.977 --> 00:03:18.183
I know you've got rainbows
coming out of your mouth.

00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:19.213
I get it.

00:03:19.213 --> 00:03:21.584
But you know, I think that's part of it.

00:03:21.584 --> 00:03:24.431
And look, and I think what's
really smart about the replay,

00:03:24.431 --> 00:03:26.744
what is it, three for
99 cents kind of thing?

00:03:26.744 --> 00:03:28.850
What I think is super smart about that is

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.460
I don't think they expect, I
don't buy anybody at Snapchat

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.980
thinking this is going to crush.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.342
Right, here's a good example.

00:03:35.342 --> 00:03:36.246
Watch this.

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:37.524
Staphon, you going to do any of it?

00:03:37.524 --> 00:03:38.556
- [Staphon] No.

00:03:38.556 --> 00:03:39.668
- DRock?

00:03:39.668 --> 00:03:40.574
- [DRock] Maybe not.

00:03:40.574 --> 00:03:42.435
- No, no, don't say what I'm leaning to.

00:03:42.435 --> 00:03:43.301
I want to know.

00:03:43.301 --> 00:03:44.617
- [DRock] No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:46.304
- [Steve] I'm going to do it once.

00:03:46.304 --> 00:03:47.212
- That makes sense.

00:03:47.212 --> 00:03:47.999
- [Steve] I want to have them

00:03:47.999 --> 00:03:49.278
standing by for emergencies.

00:03:49.278 --> 00:03:52.549
- Would emergencies be
that a lot of female

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:56.046
Vayner Nation people
find you more attractive

00:03:56.046 --> 00:03:57.820
with your new facial hair and may send you

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.015
the kind of snap that gets you

00:03:59.015 --> 00:04:00.625
to want to maybe replay it.

00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:01.660
- [Steve] That's exactly what I mean.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.776
- That's what I figured.

00:04:02.776 --> 00:04:05.776
So you know, I think
that's the cliche joke

00:04:05.776 --> 00:04:07.503
that people are going to
make about the replay.

00:04:07.503 --> 00:04:09.077
What I just did, that was on purpose.

00:04:09.077 --> 00:04:10.961
I think there will be a small subset

00:04:10.961 --> 00:04:12.612
that will do it one time.

00:04:12.612 --> 00:04:13.847
Which wouldn't be hard, I mean listen.

00:04:13.847 --> 00:04:16.071
If everybody on Snapchat does it one time,

00:04:16.071 --> 00:04:18.702
you got a 150 million
people spending a buck.

00:04:18.702 --> 00:04:20.397
That's 150 million dollars.

00:04:20.397 --> 00:04:21.839
It could add up really quick.

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:24.342
I don't expect that to be
the case, but to the point.

00:04:24.342 --> 00:04:27.519
God forbid that's the kind of play.

00:04:27.519 --> 00:04:29.790
I always say God forbid it does work.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.108
God forbid everybody does want to do it.

00:04:32.108 --> 00:04:34.377
99 cents feels right to everybody,

00:04:34.377 --> 00:04:37.972
and all of a sudden it becomes
a massive revenue stream.

00:04:37.972 --> 00:04:39.041
There was no loss.

00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:41.521
I'm a big fan of doing
things that have no downside.

00:04:41.521 --> 00:04:43.587
Now if you do a ton of features,

00:04:43.587 --> 00:04:45.189
and notice how both came out.

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:47.169
An amazing selfie feature

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:48.981
that I think everybody's going to love

00:04:48.981 --> 00:04:51.051
along with this kind
of paid kind of thing.

00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:52.088
I think it was brilliant.

00:04:52.088 --> 00:04:54.771
A really well executed update.

00:04:54.771 --> 00:04:57.719
One of my favorite updates
of the year by any platform

00:04:57.719 --> 00:04:59.677
and so what do I think about it?

00:04:59.677 --> 00:05:01.396
I don't think it's a revenue stream

00:05:01.396 --> 00:05:02.876
that is meaningful for Snapchat.

00:05:02.876 --> 00:05:05.016
I think when you take it to a higher level

00:05:05.016 --> 00:05:07.699
and think about the strategy of a update

00:05:07.699 --> 00:05:10.335
for one of the leading
consumer apps in the world,

00:05:10.335 --> 00:05:12.905
I think it's downright phenomenal.

00:05:12.905 --> 00:05:16.159
I also think that was a
downright phenomenal answer

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:18.343
and just allowed a lot of people to see

00:05:18.343 --> 00:05:19.702
that I think at a different plane

00:05:19.702 --> 00:05:22.836
which is why they're
allocating their precious time

00:05:22.836 --> 00:05:25.426
to watch the show and I appreciate that

00:05:25.426 --> 00:05:26.662
and I will continue to try to

00:05:26.662 --> 00:05:29.755
think with my God given
abilities and bring value to you.

00:05:29.755 --> 00:05:31.545
Because I do think that's
the smart conversation

00:05:31.545 --> 00:05:33.323
that people are not happening as much.

00:05:33.323 --> 00:05:34.806
As a matter of fact on that Stunwin,

00:05:34.806 --> 00:05:37.370
I want you to work with
Andy K and Sid the intern

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.561
who's in school, Sid,
good to see you brother.

00:05:39.561 --> 00:05:43.783
On an article version of this
because I think it could pop.

00:05:43.783 --> 00:05:47.058
I think you'll be seeing
this article pop later today.

00:05:47.058 --> 00:05:51.298
(popping)

00:05:53.998 --> 00:05:55.571
- What's up Gary, this is Caleb again.

00:05:55.571 --> 00:05:56.513
This time I'm not driving.

00:05:56.513 --> 00:05:57.831
However, I do have a question for you.

00:05:57.831 --> 00:06:00.053
I am developing an app with a partner.

00:06:00.053 --> 00:06:01.578
Basically the first time we built it

00:06:01.578 --> 00:06:02.935
we had an initial name and branding.

00:06:02.935 --> 00:06:04.432
However we discovered that there was

00:06:04.432 --> 00:06:05.920
a potential competitor with a similar name

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.570
so we decided to go with
another branding oppertunity

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.378
that we had, however
now there's another app

00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:10.834
with the same name and a similar premise.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.437
My overall belief is that we have

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:13.971
the superior product and
a way better strategy.

00:06:13.971 --> 00:06:15.911
My question though is do we continue

00:06:15.911 --> 00:06:17.604
to have the same name as
our potential competitor

00:06:17.604 --> 00:06:19.710
or do we completely
rebrand ourselves again

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:20.787
to find a new name.

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:21.940
What is your insights on this?

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.179
Thank you so much Gary, you're awesome.

00:06:23.179 --> 00:06:24.595
- That was amazing

00:06:24.595 --> 00:06:25.870
I love it.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.602
Man, that was amazing.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:30.719
I don't think it matters.

00:06:33.929 --> 00:06:35.887
Next question.

00:06:35.887 --> 00:06:37.369
Fine, I'll go into a little bit.

00:06:37.369 --> 00:06:38.436
You know, look.

00:06:38.436 --> 00:06:41.396
I don't think it's convenient to have

00:06:41.396 --> 00:06:43.370
a similar name with a similar
premise to a competitor.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.737
I think, you know, if Twitter

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.051
came out when Twotter came out,

00:06:46.051 --> 00:06:47.329
it would have been awkward.

00:06:47.329 --> 00:06:49.236
Especially if there was
a company named Twotter.

00:06:49.236 --> 00:06:53.515
But I think, I think that, I
think at the end of the day

00:06:53.515 --> 00:06:55.907
my point of view on this would be

00:06:55.907 --> 00:06:57.270
I'd be sitting there
and say "You know what?

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.417
"I'm just going to
out-execute the other person

00:06:59.417 --> 00:07:01.350
"and force them to change the name

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.785
"because they realize they
want to compete with us

00:07:03.785 --> 00:07:05.553
"because we were the
thing that was winning."

00:07:05.553 --> 00:07:07.451
Thought I don't love the situation.

00:07:07.451 --> 00:07:09.803
I don't want to also
say look how cool I am.

00:07:09.803 --> 00:07:11.346
I'm going to beat them to it.

00:07:11.346 --> 00:07:13.511
Like, I don't mind you
walking away from it

00:07:13.511 --> 00:07:15.188
and changing a name either.

00:07:15.188 --> 00:07:17.439
I just ultimately don't
think it's going to matter.

00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:19.558
You're going to have to out-execute.

00:07:19.558 --> 00:07:21.460
Angry Birds had a similar situation.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.083
There was a lot of birdy
kind of stuff going on.

00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:25.376
Like if you're the best
and your product's the best

00:07:25.376 --> 00:07:27.446
and you can navigate it,
you've got the right product,

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.013
and you guys are the right leaders,

00:07:29.013 --> 00:07:30.585
I don't think it ends up playing out

00:07:30.585 --> 00:07:32.607
and so I wouldn't stress
about it too much.

00:07:32.607 --> 00:07:34.910
I think a lot of times
to make it more valuable

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.533
as a question to everybody overall,

00:07:36.533 --> 00:07:38.619
I think a lot of times people
very much worry about names.

00:07:38.619 --> 00:07:40.474
I have consistently stayed on a plane

00:07:40.474 --> 00:07:41.875
of the name doesn't matter.

00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:44.510
You can make a name matter after the fact.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:46.939
I don't think Snapchat
or Facebook or Google

00:07:46.939 --> 00:07:48.454
meant anything to anybody

00:07:48.454 --> 00:07:50.060
until they actually meant something.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:51.545
You know, I guess maybe I'm affected

00:07:51.545 --> 00:07:54.110
by having a last name like Vaynerchuk.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.629
You know, it doesn't feel
like the most brandable name.

00:07:56.629 --> 00:07:58.864
I also made an incredibly huge flaw

00:07:58.864 --> 00:08:01.300
in my Twitter handle with Gary Vee.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:05.256
I mean, I have two silent
Es at the end of my username

00:08:05.256 --> 00:08:07.197
which is not easily to explain in public.

00:08:07.197 --> 00:08:09.133
It takes time every
time, time is the asset.

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:11.731
You know, people like "where's the ee?"

00:08:11.731 --> 00:08:13.214
And it just wasn't a smart move.

00:08:13.214 --> 00:08:15.237
Another bad name play by me

00:08:15.237 --> 00:08:17.220
that I think I overcame
in a Twitter environment.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.506
So execution will always trump your name.

00:08:25.456 --> 00:08:26.695
- [Steve] Stephan asks

00:08:26.695 --> 00:08:27.478
- Staphon?

00:08:27.478 --> 00:08:28.877
- [Steve] Stephan, Stephan, Stephan,

00:08:28.877 --> 00:08:29.864
we're going to go with Stephan.

00:08:29.864 --> 00:08:31.298
- All right.
- [Steve] Asks.

00:08:31.303 --> 00:08:32.660
- [Voiceover] Stephan
asks "What do you think

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:35.046
"is the strongest differentiator
between good content?

00:08:35.046 --> 00:08:36.530
"Aesthetics or copy?"

00:08:38.041 --> 00:08:38.937
- Both.

00:08:38.937 --> 00:08:43.024
You know, the variable
of success is creative,

00:08:43.024 --> 00:08:45.872
but I think the copy, the words

00:08:45.872 --> 00:08:48.597
that you support, you know,
I see it a lot on Instagram.

00:08:48.597 --> 00:08:51.188
I've tested the same
picture with different words

00:08:51.188 --> 00:08:54.321
posting at the same time of day

00:08:54.321 --> 00:08:56.013
just for my own education.

00:08:56.013 --> 00:08:59.148
And the truth is that's not
a controlled environment

00:08:59.148 --> 00:09:02.650
so it's not science, but it's anecdotal.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:03.641
It's fun to see.

00:09:03.641 --> 00:09:05.003
I mean clearly the words,

00:09:05.003 --> 00:09:06.938
some people are going to react,

00:09:06.938 --> 00:09:09.179
and the reason I brought
up Instagram to everybody

00:09:09.179 --> 00:09:11.641
is we all know that Instagram
is massively visual.

00:09:11.641 --> 00:09:13.993
But people still read the copy.

00:09:13.993 --> 00:09:16.497
I mean this is crazy, I saw
somebody at a conference

00:09:16.497 --> 00:09:17.816
giving advice that you shouldn't

00:09:17.816 --> 00:09:19.717
write long form copy on Instagram.

00:09:19.717 --> 00:09:22.023
And I was laughing because
it's just a simplistic answer.

00:09:22.023 --> 00:09:23.509
I actually think long form copy

00:09:23.509 --> 00:09:25.708
is one of the big arbitrage
opportunities on Instagram.

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:29.496
And so I think they equally matter.

00:09:29.496 --> 00:09:32.177
I think you'll get results predicated

00:09:32.177 --> 00:09:33.415
on where your strengths lie.

00:09:33.415 --> 00:09:35.479
I'm not very good at the picture stuff.

00:09:35.479 --> 00:09:37.332
I'm not really even
good at the copy stuff.

00:09:37.332 --> 00:09:38.695
I'm really good at the video stuff.

00:09:38.695 --> 00:09:41.503
So that's it, you know.

00:09:41.503 --> 00:09:43.533
That to me is, the answer's both.

00:09:43.533 --> 00:09:44.804
And it will always be both.

00:09:44.804 --> 00:09:46.455
And it's happened so much.

00:09:46.455 --> 00:09:47.774
Just do it.

00:09:47.774 --> 00:09:51.570
What was, you know, was
that the three words?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.287
Or was it the awesome
imagery that came along

00:09:54.287 --> 00:09:56.228
with the initial kind of campaign?

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:58.663
Was it Beau Jackson like this?

00:09:58.663 --> 00:10:01.155
Or was it the slogan?

00:10:01.155 --> 00:10:02.420
I mean there's always that.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.480
I mean, would priceless
from MasterCard pop

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:10.030
if the first video wasn't
emotionally rippling and got you?

00:10:11.269 --> 00:10:12.685
So the answer is both.

00:10:12.685 --> 00:10:14.700
You need both to be, you know,

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.610
